sentences.l:
and in no way ought I,
in another’s house, wailing and lamenting,
to sit, since it is worse to mourn without end, always;

“Stranger, truly my excellence, both form and body,
the immortals destroyed, when to Ilium they were going up,
the Argives, and among them my husband went, Odysseus;
if he, having come, were to tend my life,
greater would my fame be and finer, thus.

A robe, first, some power breathed into my wits for me,
who had set up a great loom, to weave in the halls,
fine and very large;

and greatly my parents urge me
to marry, and the child is vexed at their devouring his livelihood,
understanding it;

for that is the way of it, whenever from the fatherland
his own he is away, a man, for so long a time as I now,
over many cities of mortals wandering, suffering pains;

and among them Cnossus, a great city, where Minos
nine-yeared reigned, of great Zeus the confidant,
father of my father, of great-hearted Deucalion;
and Deucalion begot me and lord Idomeneus;

But he, in curved ships, to Ilium within
went off with the sons of Atreus, and to me the name, famous, is Aethon,
the younger by birth;

and to his other companions, who followed along with him,
from the land barley-meal I gave and fire-faced wine, having collected it,
and oxen to slaughter, so that they might fill their heart.
